      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Find help page about buying tickets.",
        "memory_description": "For tasks requiring locating a help page about a specific topic, prioritize navigating through primary navigation menus and using direct links to support sections.",
        "content_body": "1. Identify the main navigation menu or header of the website. Look for a section labeled 'Help', 'Support', or 'FAQ'.\n2. Click on the relevant support section link (e.g., 'Help' or 'Support').\n3. On the help/support page, search for or navigate to a subsection related to the specific topic (e.g., 'Buying Tickets').\n4. If a search box is present, TYPE the topic (e.g., 'buying tickets') and wait for the autocomplete dropdown to appear before CLICKing the most relevant suggestion.\n5. If no search box is present, scan the page for links or headings that match the topic and CLICK the appropriate link.\n6. Avoid clicking on unrelated links or sections that do not directly address the task goal. Ensure that each step leads closer to the specific help content required."
      }
