      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Find a private room in New York for 1 April and checkout on 2 April for 2 adults",
        "memory_description": "Accommodation search task failed due to incorrect date input sequence and missing UI interaction for guest count; fix by entering check-in date first, then check-out date, and explicitly selecting guest count.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Accommodation Search (Airbnb)\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Click on the 'Where' field (e.g., element ID [748]) and type 'New York' into the search box (element ID [19227]).\n2. Click on the 'Check-in' date field (element ID [29005]) and type '1 April' (format: DD MMM).\n3. Click on the 'Check-out' date field (element ID [39449]) and type '2 April' (format: DD MMM).\n4. Click on the 'Guests' field (element ID [50313]) to open the guest selector.\n5. Click on the 'Adults' section (element ID [61626]) and select '2' adults.\n6. Confirm the selection by clicking the 'Done' or 'Apply' button (element ID [70662] or similar).\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Dates must be entered in the format 'DD MMM' (e.g., '1 April', '2 April').\n- Guest count must be explicitly selected via the guest selector UI, not by typing directly into the field.\n- Ensure all steps are completed in the correct order: location, check-in, check-out, guests."
      }
