      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Look for a business class flight to Paris from Salt Lake City on June 2, with a return on June 7, and checkout",
        "memory_description": "This is a flight booking task where the agent failed to correctly select the origin city, leading to task failure; the correct workflow requires precise input of departure and arrival cities, correct date selection, and proper navigation through the booking process.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Flight Booking\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the JetBlue homepage and click on the 'Book a Flight' option.\n2. In the origin field, type 'Salt Lake City' and select the correct city from the dropdown list.\n3. In the destination field, type 'Paris' and select the correct city from the dropdown list.\n4. Select the departure date as June 2 using the date picker.\n5. Select the return date as June 7 using the date picker.\n6. Ensure the class is set to 'Business' by clicking on the class selection dropdown and choosing 'Business Class'.\n7. Click 'Search Flights' to view available options.\n8. Select a suitable flight from the results and proceed to checkout by clicking 'Continue' or 'Book Now'.\n9. Complete the checkout process by entering passenger details, payment information, and confirming the booking.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Always verify that the correct city is selected from the dropdown after typing.\n- Use the date picker to ensure accurate date selection.\n- Confirm the class selection before proceeding to search.\n- Follow the step-by-step prompts on the page to avoid skipping critical steps."
      }
