      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Look for an intern career within Newegg in City of Industry, California, USA, and bookmark it.",
        "memory_description": "Career search task failed due to incorrect element selection during navigation; correct workflow requires precise use of search filters and proper bookmarking.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Career Search and Bookmarking\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the Newegg careers page (e.g., via homepage menu or direct URL: https://www.newegg.com/careers).\n2. Use the search/filter bar to input 'intern' as the job title, 'City of Industry' as the location, and 'California, USA' as the state/country.\n3. Wait for the job list to load, then click on the first relevant intern job listing (ensure the job title and location match the criteria).\n4. Once on the job detail page, click the 'Bookmark' or 'Save' button (typically located in the top-right corner of the page or under job actions).\n5. Confirm the bookmark is saved (e.g., via a notification or bookmark icon change).\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Use precise text-based search inputs (e.g., 'intern', 'City of Industry', 'California, USA') to filter results.\n- Ensure the correct job listing is selected by verifying the title and location before proceeding.\n- Bookmarking must be done on the job detail page, not the search results page.\n- Use explicit action syntax: `CLICK [element_id]` where `element_id` corresponds to the correct UI element (e.g., search input, job title, bookmark button)."
      }
