        "scenario_description": "What are the family rides available at frontier city?",
        "memory_description": "This was a web search task where the agent failed to correctly navigate to the family rides section at Frontier City due to incorrect initial element selection, requiring a revised action sequence to ensure accurate navigation.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Web Navigation (Search for specific content on a website)\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the 'Frontier City' section of the Six Flags website.\n2. Locate and click on the 'Rides' or 'Attractions' menu item (ensure correct element selection using unique identifiers or text content).\n3. Look for a 'Family Rides' filter or category and click on it.\n4. Scroll through or select the list of family-friendly rides displayed.\n5. Extract the names of the rides and confirm they are labeled as family-friendly.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Use precise element identifiers (e.g., text content or unique IDs) to ensure correct selection.\n- Verify that each click action corresponds to the intended UI element (e.g., buttons, links, or filters).\n- If a filter is not immediately visible, look for a 'View All' or 'More Options' link to expand ride categories.\n\nCorrect Action Sequence (Syntax):\n[CLICK [1058]] -> [CLICK [12071]] -> [CLICK [21796]] -> [CLICK [29735]] -> [CLICK [41756]]"
      }
