      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Find the top rated indie rock music track and set the track as current obsession and after that watch all other obsessions too.",
        "memory_description": "This was a web navigation task where the agent failed due to incorrect element selection and missing steps in interacting with the 'current obsession' and 'watch all other obsessions' features on last.fm.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Web Navigation with UI Interaction\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the 'Indie Rock' genre page on last.fm.\n2. Locate and click on the 'Top Rated' section to view the highest-rated tracks.\n3. Identify the top-rated track and click on it to open the track page.\n4. On the track page, locate and click the 'Set as Current Obsession' button (typically found in the track actions or sidebar).\n5. After setting the track as current obsession, navigate to the 'Obsessions' section (usually in the user profile or sidebar).\n6. Click the 'Watch All Other Obsessions' button to view and interact with other obsessions.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Use precise element identifiers (e.g., button text, class names, or unique IDs) when clicking.\n- Ensure each action is validated by checking for the correct page transition or state change.\n- If a target element is not found, re-evaluate the current page structure and re-locate the correct element."
      }
