        "scenario_description": "Choose a car which is closest to 10001 New York City for 1 day.",
        "memory_description": "Location-based car rental task failed due to incorrect ZIP code input and wrong element selection; fix by using correct ZIP format and following precise UI interaction steps.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Location-based car rental selection.\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Open the car rental website (budget).\n2. Locate the 'Pickup Location' or 'ZIP Code' input field (ensure it accepts ZIP codes, not full addresses).\n3. Type the correct ZIP code: `10001` (not `10001 New York City`).\n4. Select the 'Pickup Date' and set it to today's date.\n5. Set the 'Rental Duration' to 1 day.\n6. Click the 'Search' or 'Find Cars' button to view available options.\n7. Choose the car that is closest to the location (based on displayed distance or availability).\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Use exact ZIP code format (e.g., `10001`) without additional text.\n- Ensure all actions (CLICK, TYPE) are applied to the correct UI elements as identified by their unique IDs or labels.\n- Confirm each step matches the target action and element to avoid mismatches."
