        "scenario_description": "Add the pre made College Supply List to my list.",
        "memory_description": "The task was a web navigation task to add a pre-made College Supply List to a user's list, but it failed due to an initial step where the target element was not found in the cleaned HTML, likely due to dynamic content loading or incorrect element identification.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Web Navigation (UI Interaction)\n\nCorrective Strategy:\n1. Ensure the page is fully loaded before attempting to interact with elements, especially if dynamic content is involved.\n2. Use explicit waits or checks for the presence of the target element (e.g., 'pre-made College Supply List') before attempting to click it.\n3. Correct Action Sequence:\n   a. Navigate to the Menards website and search for 'College Supply List'.\n   b. Wait for the list to load and locate the 'Add to My List' button (ensure the element is present in the DOM).\n   c. Click the 'Add to My List' button using the correct element identifier (e.g., CLICK [554] if it's the correct ID).\n   d. Confirm the addition by checking the user's list or receiving a success message.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Always verify the presence of the target element before performing an action.\n- Use element IDs or XPath that are stable and not prone to change.\n- If dynamic content is involved, implement waits or polling mechanisms to ensure the element is available."
      }
