      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Search for \"you are Amazing\" congrats gift card which can be printed and folded at home, priced between 50 and 100, and add two 50-dollar cards to the cart.",
        "memory_description": "Search task failed due to incorrect initial search input and missing price filter application; correct by typing the full search query and applying price filters before selecting items.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Web Search & Product Selection\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to Amazon's search bar (typically located at the top of the page).\n2. TYPE [search_box] [\"you are Amazing\" congrats gift card printable foldable]\n3. Wait for search results to load.\n4. Locate and CLICK [price_filter_button] to open the price filter panel.\n5. SET [price_min] [50] and SET [price_max] [100] to filter results within the desired price range.\n6. Scroll through filtered results and CLICK [product_card] for a gift card priced at $50 that is marked as printable/foldable.\n7. CLICK [add_to_cart_button] to add the first card to the cart.\n8. RETURN to the search results and repeat step 6 to find a second $50 gift card.\n9. CLICK [add_to_cart_button] again to add the second card to the cart.\n10. CONFIRM that two items are in the cart by CLICK [cart_icon].\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Use exact text for search queries to match product titles.\n- Apply price filters before selecting items to avoid irrelevant results.\n- Ensure the product is explicitly marked as printable/foldable before adding to cart."
