      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Find discussions of community and open one with most replies.",
        "memory_description": "This was a forum navigation task where the agent failed to correctly identify and interact with the discussion threads related to 'community' and select the one with the most replies due to incorrect element targeting.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Forum Navigation\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the 'Community' or 'Discussions' section of the FlightAware website.\n2. Locate the list of discussion threads using a selector like `div.thread-list` or similar.\n3. Filter or search for threads containing the keyword 'community' using a search box or filter input (e.g., `input[type='search']` or `input[name='q']`).\n4. Once the relevant threads are displayed, sort them by the number of replies (e.g., by clicking a 'Replies' column header or using a dropdown filter like `select[name='sort']` with value 'replies').\n5. Click on the first or topmost thread in the sorted list using an action like `CLICK [thread-title-element]` where the element is identified by a unique attribute or class (e.g., `a.thread-title` or `div.thread-item`).\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Always verify that the element clicked corresponds to a discussion thread (e.g., contains text like 'community' and has a reply count).\n- Use explicit selectors (e.g., `a.thread-title` or `div.thread-item`) to ensure correct element targeting.\n- Confirm that the sorting/filtering action is applied before selecting a thread."
      }
