        "scenario_description": "Set the first recommended song on the homepage as a current obsession",
        "memory_description": "A navigation task on last.fm failed due to incorrect element selection and missing interaction steps; the correct workflow requires locating the first recommended song and using the 'Add to Obsessions' button.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Web Navigation (UI Interaction)\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the homepage of last.fm.\n2. Locate the first recommended song in the 'Recommended' section (typically under a carousel or list).\n3. Click on the song to open its detail page.\n4. Look for the 'Add to Obsessions' button (usually a heart icon or a button labeled 'Add to Obsessions') and click it.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Ensure the first recommended song is selected by verifying its position in the DOM or visual hierarchy.\n- Use explicit selectors for the 'Add to Obsessions' button, such as `button[data-action='add-to-obsessions']` or similar.\n- Confirm the action is completed by checking for a success message or visual feedback (e.g., the heart icon turns red)."
      }
