      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Find Chevrolet Silverado with black exterior color and maximum value of $30,000.",
        "memory_description": "Filter-based search task failed due to incorrect element selection and missing steps for applying filters; correct workflow requires precise use of search and filter UI elements.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Filter-based search on a vehicle inventory website (carmax). \n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the search bar and type `Chevrolet Silverado` using `TYPE [191] [Chevrolet Silverado]`.\n2. Click on the search results or 'Search' button using `CLICK [5631]`.\n3. Locate and click on the 'Exterior Color' filter dropdown using `CLICK [10706]`.\n4. Select 'Black' from the color options using `CLICK [33106]`.\n5. Locate and click on the 'Price' filter dropdown using `CLICK [54048]`.\n6. Set the maximum price to `$30,000` using `CLICK [76159]`.\n7. Apply the filters by clicking 'Apply' or 'Search Again' using `CLICK [98023]`.\n8. Review the filtered results using `CLICK [119958]`.\n9. Confirm the results meet the criteria using `CLICK [141209]`.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Always verify the correct element ID matches the target action.\n- Ensure filter values are explicitly set (e.g., 'Black' for color, '$30,000' for price).\n- Use exact syntax: `TYPE [element_id] [value]` and `CLICK [element_id]`."
      }
