      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Search for a full-time job in sales in Springfield and apply for the most recent job.",
        "memory_description": "Job search task on Carmax failed due to incorrect element selection and missing click actions; correct workflow requires precise navigation and interaction with job search filters and application buttons.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Job Search and Application\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the 'Careers' or 'Jobs' section of the Carmax website.\n2. Locate the job search filter or input field (e.g., 'Job Title' or 'Location') and type 'sales' into the job title field.\n3. In the location field, type 'Springfield' and select it from the dropdown or search results.\n4. Ensure the 'Full-time' employment filter is selected.\n5. Click the 'Search' or 'Find Jobs' button to load available positions.\n6. From the list of results, click on the most recent job posting (e.g., the first item in the list or a 'Most Recent' filter option if available).\n7. On the job details page, locate and click the 'Apply Now' or 'Apply' button to submit the application.\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Use 'CLICK' for buttons and links.\n- Use 'TYPE' for text input fields.\n- Use 'SELECT' for dropdowns with explicit value selection.\n- Ensure each step matches the exact element ID and action type as defined in the website's DOM structure."
      }
