      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Find Auto train going from Moynihan to Chicago IL leaving on April 22nd to 29th for 2 adult.",
        "memory_description": "This is a train booking task where the agent failed to correctly select UI elements for date range and passenger selection, leading to an incomplete or incorrect search.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Train Booking (Auto Train Search)\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the Amtrak homepage and click on the 'Find Trains' or 'Book Tickets' button (element ID: 187).\n2. In the departure station field, type 'Moynihan' and select the correct station from the dropdown (element ID: 11740).\n3. In the arrival station field, type 'Chicago IL' and select the correct station from the dropdown (element ID: 41646).\n4. Click on the date field and select a date range from April 22nd to April 29th (element ID: 52999, value: 'April 22 - April 29').\n5. Click on the 'Passengers' field and select '2 adults' (element ID: 82892).\n6. Click the 'Search' or 'Find Trains' button (element ID: 98141).\n7. Review the results and select the 'Auto Train' option if available (element ID: 113723).\n8. Confirm the booking details and proceed with payment if needed (element ID: 128969, 144251, 159808).\n9. Finalize the booking by clicking the 'Book Now' or 'Confirm' button (element ID: 175071, 190280, 205642).\nUI Interaction Rules: Always verify the correct element ID and value before clicking or typing. Use exact date ranges and passenger counts as specified in the task."
      }
