      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Book an interior room for over 10 days on a cruise for two people from Brisbane to Papua New Guinea leaving November 2024. Check out with default options and pay in full.",
        "memory_description": "Cruise booking task failed due to incorrect element selection during passenger details and cabin selection steps; correct by following precise UI interaction rules and ensuring exact element targeting.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Cruise Booking\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the 'Cruises' section and select a cruise departing from Brisbane to Papua New Guinea in November 2024 with a duration of over 10 days.\n2. Click on 'Book Now' or equivalent to start the booking process.\n3. Enter passenger details: select '2 adults' and ensure the correct dropdown or input field is used (e.g., CLICK [5541] for passenger count).\n4. Proceed to cabin selection: click on 'Interior' cabin type (e.g., CLICK [39116] for interior room selection).\n5. Confirm the booking with default options (e.g., CLICK [58030] to confirm cabin selection).\n6. Proceed to checkout and select 'Pay in Full' (e.g., CLICK [74248] to confirm payment method).\n7. Finalize the booking by clicking 'Complete Booking' or equivalent (e.g., CLICK [81492]).\nUI Interaction Rules: Always verify the exact element ID and action type (CLICK/SELECT) from the HTML. Use CLICK for buttons and SELECT for dropdowns with [value] syntax."
      }
