        "content_body": "Task Type: Job Search on Website (Target)\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the job search page (e.g., 'Careers' or 'Jobs' section).\n2. Locate and click the 'Search' or 'Find Jobs' button to open the job search interface.\n3. In the search bar, type 'Human Resources' as the job title.\n4. Use the location filter and select 'Miami, Florida' from the dropdown or search field.\n5. Click the 'Search' or 'Apply Filters' button to execute the job search.\n6. Review the job listings displayed in the results section.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Use `CLICK [element_id]` only when the element_id corresponds to a visible and actionable UI component (e.g., search bar, dropdown, button).\n- Ensure the action value (e.g., 'Human Resources', 'Miami, Florida') is correctly formatted and matches the expected input format of the field.\n- Verify that each step's element is present in the cleaned HTML before executing the action.\n\nCorrect Action Sequence Example:\nCLICK [1859] (search bar)\nTYPE 'Human Resources'\nCLICK [2492] (location field)\nTYPE 'Miami, Florida'\nCLICK [536939] (search button)"
      }
