      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Find 2 tickets to see the New York Yankees play on March 30, 2023 and filter to show price including fees.",
        "memory_description": "Ticket purchase task failed due to incorrect selection of a dropdown instead of clicking a button; correct workflow requires clicking the 'Select' button rather than using a SELECT action on the dropdown element.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Ticket Purchase\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the event search page for the New York Yankees on March 30, 2023.\n2. Click on the search or event listing element (e.g., CLICK [96]).\n3. Scroll to the ticket selection section and click on the 'Select' button (e.g., CLICK [13976]).\n4. Avoid using SELECT actions on dropdowns; instead, click the 'Select' or 'Apply' button to proceed (e.g., CLICK [27886], not SELECT [27886] [2]).\n5. Filter the results to show prices including fees by clicking the appropriate filter option (e.g., CLICK [42988]).\n6. Confirm the selection of 2 tickets and complete the purchase or view the results (e.g., CLICK [58772]).\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Use CLICK actions for buttons and links, not SELECT for dropdowns.\n- Ensure all steps match the exact element IDs and actions in the HTML.\n- Always verify that the action corresponds to the correct UI element (e.g., 'Select' button vs. dropdown menu)."
      }
