        "content_body": "Task Type: Web Search (Used Car Filter)\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the 'Make' dropdown and SELECT [Honda].\n2. Navigate to the 'Model' dropdown and SELECT [Crosstour].\n3. Navigate to the 'ZIP Code' field and TYPE [49102].\n4. Click the 'Search' button to apply location and model filters.\n5. In the 'Year' filter, first SELECT [2013], then SELECT [2012] to include both years.\n6. Apply the 'Price' filter by setting the maximum value to less than $25,000.\n7. Finally, click the 'Sort by' dropdown and SELECT [Lowest mileage first] to get the desired results.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Always apply year filters in descending order (newest first) to ensure all desired years are included.\n- Confirm that all filters (make, model, year, price, location) are applied before sorting.\n- Use exact dropdown values as displayed on the page (e.g., '2013' and '2012' must be selected individually)."
