      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Find a new drone priced between 25 to 50 dollar and ships from USA with average customer rating of 4 and upwards and save the search at the end.",
        "memory_description": "Product search task on Newegg failed due to incorrect element selection and missing filter application steps; correct workflow requires precise use of search, filter, and save actions with accurate UI element targeting.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Product Search and Filter on E-commerce Site (Newegg)\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. `TYPE [126] [drone]` - Type 'drone' into the search bar.\n2. `CLICK [41868]` - Click the 'Search' button to initiate the search.\n3. `CLICK [59674]` - Click on the 'Price' filter option.\n4. `CLICK [108328]` - Click on the 'Price Range' input field.\n5. `SELECT [145740] [25-50]` - Select the price range '25-50' from the dropdown or input field.\n6. `CLICK [195063]` - Click on the 'Ship From' filter option.\n7. `CLICK [232865]` - Click on the 'USA' option under the 'Ship From' filter.\n8. `CLICK [278868]` - Click on the 'Customer Rating' filter option.\n9. `SELECT [306282] [4]` - Select the rating '4' or higher from the dropdown.\n10. `CLICK [359240]` - Click the 'Apply Filters' button to apply all selected criteria.\n11. `CLICK [412165]` - Click on a product that matches the criteria (e.g., first item in results).\n12. `SELECT [448601] [Lowest Price]` - Select the 'Lowest Price' option if available for sorting.\n13. `CLICK [461924]` - Click the 'Save Search' or 'Save Results' button to save the search.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Always verify the correct element ID before clicking or selecting.\n- Use `SELECT` for dropdowns and `CLICK` for buttons or checkboxes.\n- Ensure all filters are applied sequentially and confirmed before proceeding."
      }
