      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Find information about what I should do when I lose an item on a bus.",
        "memory_description": "For tasks requiring finding information about lost items on a bus, the key workflow insight is to directly navigate to the relevant help or FAQ section using known menu items.",
        "content_body": "1. Identify the main navigation menu or help section on the website, typically found in the header or footer. 2. Look for a menu item related to 'Help', 'FAQ', 'Lost Items', or 'Contact Us'. 3. Click on the relevant link that addresses lost items or customer support. 4. If a dropdown or submenu appears, wait for it to fully load before selecting the appropriate option. 5. Ensure that the selected link leads to a page with detailed instructions or contact information for lost items. Decision points: If no direct link is available, use a search box (if present) to type 'lost item' or similar terms, then click on the most relevant result. Common pitfalls: Avoid clicking on unrelated links or ads that may lead to incorrect information."
      }
