      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Find a campground in Orlando for 2 adults to check-in in mar 29 and check out in mar 30",
        "memory_description": "Search task failed due to incorrect interaction with location input and missing click on search button; correct by typing location and explicitly clicking search.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Search for a campground with specific check-in/check-out dates.\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the main search page of the website.\n2. Locate the 'Location' input field (e.g., with ID or class name 'location-input') and type 'Orlando' into it.\n3. Find the 'Check-in' date input field (e.g., with ID or class name 'check-in-date') and click it, then select or type 'Mar 29'.\n4. Find the 'Check-out' date input field (e.g., with ID or class name 'check-out-date') and click it, then select or type 'Mar 30'.\n5. Locate the 'Number of Guests' selector (e.g., with ID or class name 'guests-selector') and select '2 adults'.\n6. Find and click the 'Search' or 'Find Campgrounds' button (e.g., with ID or class name 'search-button') to submit the query.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Always verify that the correct element is selected before interacting.\n- Use 'CLICK' for buttons and 'TYPE' for text inputs.\n- Ensure that all required fields (location, dates, guests) are filled before submitting the search."
