      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Check all available one way flights for a single passenger from Manhattan to Philadelphia on May 23rd in first class.",
        "memory_description": "Flight search task failed due to incorrect selection of the class option; the correct action is to click the class option instead of selecting it with a value.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Flight Search\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the Delta Airlines website.\n2. Click on the 'Flights' tab or search button to initiate a flight search.\n3. In the origin field, type 'Manhattan' and select the correct location from the dropdown.\n4. In the destination field, type 'Philadelphia' and select the correct location from the dropdown.\n5. Set the departure date to May 23rd using the date picker.\n6. Ensure the number of passengers is set to 1.\n7. Click on the 'Class' dropdown and select 'First Class' by clicking the appropriate option (do not use a SELECT action with a value, use CLICK on the class option itself).\n8. Submit the search to view available flights."
      }
