      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Find one way flights for one person from Sacramento to Houston IAH on June 2, 2023 that can be booked using miles.",
        "memory_description": "Flight search task failed due to incorrect initial element selection and missing input for origin, destination, and date; correct workflow requires precise input of origin, destination, date, and selection of miles-based booking option.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Flight Search (One-way, Miles Booking)\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Open the flight booking page on the 'united' website.\n2. Locate and click on the 'From' field (ensure correct element is selected, e.g., [8790]).\n3. Type 'Sacramento' into the 'From' field (e.g., TYPE [8790] [Sacramento]).\n4. Locate and click on the 'To' field (e.g., [34900]).\n5. Type 'Houston IAH' into the 'To' field (e.g., TYPE [34900] [Houston IAH]).\n6. Locate and click on the 'Departure Date' field (e.g., [52374]).\n7. Select or type 'June 2, 2023' into the date field (e.g., TYPE [52374] [June 2, 2023]).\n8. Locate and click on the 'Miles' or 'Book with Miles' option (e.g., [62788]).\n9. Confirm the search by clicking the 'Search' or 'Find Flights' button (e.g., [71931]).\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Ensure correct element IDs are used for each input field (e.g., [8790] for origin, [34900] for destination, [52374] for date).\n- Use the correct syntax: CLICK [element_id] or TYPE [element_id] [value].\n- Always verify that the element exists in the cleaned HTML before interacting with it."
      }
