      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Search for parking near restaurants in Boston and find a parking spot near Hard Rock Cafe for an oversized car from 9 to 11 pm on May 11, and ensure that the pre-purchase and open gate with phone option is available.",
        "memory_description": "This is a multi-step web navigation task where the agent failed to correctly identify and interact with UI elements, leading to incorrect clicks and missed steps in the parking search workflow.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Multi-step Web Navigation (Parking Search with Specific Filters)\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the parking website and locate the search bar (e.g., by clicking on a 'Search' or 'Find Parking' button).\n2. Type 'Hard Rock Cafe' into the search field to filter results near the restaurant.\n3. Select the location or confirm the address for Hard Rock Cafe in Boston.\n4. Set the date to May 11 and time from 9 to 11 PM using the respective date/time pickers or input fields.\n5. Choose the 'Oversized Car' option from the vehicle size filter dropdown or toggle.\n6. Ensure the 'Pre-purchase' and 'Open Gate with Phone' options are selected by clicking the corresponding checkboxes or toggles.\n7. Submit the search or click 'Find Parking' to view available spots.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Use `CLICK [element_id]` for buttons and links.\n- Use `TYPE [element_id] [value]` for text inputs (e.g., `TYPE [2263] [hard rock cafe]`).\n- Use `SELECT [element_id] [option]` for dropdowns or toggles (e.g., `SELECT [39052] [ON]` for enabling a feature).\n- Always verify the element ID matches the target before interacting."
      }
    },
