      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Look for outdoor parking in Arlington, Virgina near 5601 Chapin Ave, Alexandria, where I can pay with my phone and charge my car on April 27 from 10 am to April 28, 10 am.",
        "memory_description": "The task was a location-based search for outdoor parking with specific payment and charging requirements; the agent failed due to incorrect element selection during critical steps, particularly when navigating filters and selecting options.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Location-based search for outdoor parking with specific filters (phone payment, charging, date/time).\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the parking search page.\n2. Enter the address: `TYPE [search_box] [5601 Chapin Ave, Alexandria, Virginia]`.\n3. Select the location from the dropdown or map results: `CLICK [location_result]`.\n4. Set the date range: `CLICK [date_picker]` → `TYPE [start_date] [April 27]` → `TYPE [end_date] [April 28]`.\n5. Set the time range: `CLICK [time_picker]` → `TYPE [start_time] [10:00 AM]` → `TYPE [end_time] [10:00 AM]`.\n6. Apply filters: `CLICK [filters]` → `CLICK [outdoor_parking]` → `CLICK [phone_payment]` → `CLICK [charging]`.\n7. Submit the search: `CLICK [search_button]`.\n8. Review results and select a suitable parking option: `CLICK [result_item]`.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Always verify that the element clicked corresponds to the intended action (e.g., a location result, date picker, or filter option).\n- Use precise syntax for typing values (e.g., `TYPE [element] [value]` with exact formatting).\n- Ensure all filters are explicitly applied before submitting the search."
      }
