      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Open the baggage fee calculator.",
        "memory_description": "For tasks requiring accessing a baggage fee calculator, a direct sequence of clicks on specific UI elements is effective.",
        "content_body": "To open a baggage fee calculator on a website, follow this step-by-step workflow:\n\n1. Identify and click on the primary navigation element that leads to baggage-related information (e.g., a 'Baggage' or 'Fees' menu item). Ensure the element is correctly selected based on its label or position.\n2. Locate and click on a sub-menu or link that explicitly mentions 'Baggage Fee Calculator' or a similar label. This step may appear in a dropdown or sidebar after the first click.\n3. Click on the final element that opens the calculator, which may be a button or link labeled 'Calculate' or 'View Baggage Fees'.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Always confirm that the target element is fully loaded and visible before clicking to avoid errors.\n- If dropdowns or modals appear, wait for them to fully render before interacting with their contents.\n\nPitfalls to Avoid:\n- Do not assume the same element IDs or labels will be present on different websites; always verify the element's context and label.\n- Ensure that each click leads to the next logical step in the workflow; if a page reloads or redirects unexpectedly, re-evaluate the sequence."
      }
    },
