        "scenario_description": "Book the lowest-priced train or bus from Alexandria, Washington to Penn Station, New York, on May 3 for a single traveler.",
        "memory_description": "This is a multi-step travel booking task where incorrect element selection and partial input caused failure; the correct workflow requires precise element targeting and exact input formatting.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Multi-step travel booking (train or bus)\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. CLICK [501] (search button or travel option selector)\n2. CLICK [4420] (transportation type selector: train or bus)\n3. CLICK [15972] (origin input field)\n4. TYPE [20033] [ALEXANDRIA] (exact city name, no state abbreviation)\n5. CLICK [31559] (destination input field)\n6. TYPE [35686] [PENN STATION] (exact station name)\n7. CLICK [47296] (date selector or calendar)\n8. CLICK [51395] (date: May 3)\n9. CLICK [59393] (passenger selector or single traveler option)\n10. CLICK [67810] (search or find tickets button)\n11. CLICK [75191] (lowest-priced option selector)\n12. CLICK [97197] (confirm or book button)\n13. CLICK [123297] (final confirmation or payment step)\n14. CLICK [151502] (complete booking or finish transaction)\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Use exact city names (e.g., 'ALEXANDRIA' not 'Alexandria, Washington')\n- Select the correct element IDs as specified in the target\n- Ensure all input values match the expected format (e.g., station names, dates)\n- Follow the exact sequence of steps to avoid missing critical selection or input steps."
      }
