      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Show me schedules for the Blue water route on Wednesdays",
        "memory_description": "This was a schedule lookup task on Amtrak's website; the agent failed to select the correct route and date filter options, leading to incomplete or incorrect results.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Schedule Lookup\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the Amtrak homepage and click on the 'Schedules' or 'Find Trains' option.\n2. In the search form, select the 'Blue Water' route from the 'Route' dropdown menu.\n3. Set the 'From' and 'To' fields to the appropriate stations for the Blue Water route (e.g., Detroit to Port Huron).\n4. In the 'Date' field, select 'Wednesday' or enter a specific Wednesday date.\n5. Click the 'Find Trains' or 'Search' button to retrieve the schedule.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Ensure the correct route name ('Blue Water') is selected from the route dropdown.\n- Use the date picker or manually input a Wednesday date to filter results.\n- Confirm that the 'Find Trains' button is clicked after all filters are applied.\n\nCorrect Action Sequence (Syntax):\nCLICK [3101] -> CLICK [39292] -> CLICK [52408] -> CLICK [80330]"
      }
