      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Look up round trip flights for 1 person to Japan at the Narita airport departing on 6/16 and returning on 6/23.",
        "memory_description": "Round trip flight lookup task failed due to incorrect element selection; correct workflow requires precise UI interaction with destination, dates, and airport fields.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Round trip flight lookup on kayak.com\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Open kayak.com and navigate to the flight search section.\n2. In the 'From' field, type and select the departure city (e.g., 'New York') using `CLICK [element_id]` where the element contains the correct city name.\n3. In the 'To' field, type and select 'Narita, Japan' using `CLICK [element_id]` where the element contains 'Narita' and 'Japan'.\n4. Click on the departure date field and select '6/16' using `CLICK [element_id]` where the element corresponds to the calendar date picker for June 16.\n5. Click on the return date field and select '6/23' using `CLICK [element_id]` where the element corresponds to the calendar date picker for June 23.\n6. Ensure the number of passengers is set to 1 using `CLICK [element_id]` where the element corresponds to the passenger count selector.\n7. Submit the search using `CLICK [element_id]` where the element is the 'Search Flights' button."
      }
