      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Find a car to rent in Detroit, MI for pick up on April 2 and drop-off on April 3, both at 11AM, only show cars from Enterprise and Avis",
        "memory_description": "A car rental search task failed due to incorrect city input and missing brand filter steps; fix by entering 'Detroit' without state and explicitly selecting Enterprise and Avis.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Car Rental Search\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the car rental website (e.g., rentalcars.com).\n2. Locate and click on the 'Pickup City' input field.\n3. Type `Detroit` (without the state abbreviation) into the field.\n4. Select the 'Pickup Date' field and set it to April 2.\n5. Select the 'Drop-off Date' field and set it to April 3.\n6. Set both 'Pickup Time' and 'Drop-off Time' to `11:00 AM`.\n7. Locate the 'Brand' or 'Rental Company' filter section.\n8. Click on the filter dropdown and select both `Enterprise` and `Avis`.\n9. Click the 'Search' or 'Find Cars' button to view results.\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Use exact city names without state abbreviations.\n- Ensure time format is `11:00 AM` (not `11 00 AM`).\n- Always explicitly select required brands in the filter options."
      }
