      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Get cheapest medium car with like for like fuel policy from the Boston airport shuttle at 4 pm on April 16th and drop it off the next day at 3:30 pm,if booking is not available on that day, move the booking a day further and try to book again\n.",
        "memory_description": "This is a web booking task where the agent failed to correctly identify and click on the appropriate fuel policy option, leading to a failed booking workflow.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Web Booking (Car Rental)\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the 'Rental Cars' website and select the 'Book a Car' option.\n2. Choose the pickup location as 'Boston Airport' and set the pickup time to '4:00 PM' on April 16th.\n3. Set the drop-off location as 'Boston Airport' and the drop-off time to '3:30 PM' on April 17th.\n4. Select the car type as 'Medium' and ensure the fuel policy is set to 'Like for Like' (look for a dropdown or checkbox labeled 'Like for Like' or 'Fuel Policy' and select it).\n5. Click the 'Search' or 'Find Cars' button to view available options.\n6. If no cars are available, increment the drop-off date by one day (April 18th) and repeat steps 4-6.\n7. Once a car is found, click 'Book Now' and complete the booking process.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Use SELECT [element_id] [value] for dropdown selections (e.g., SELECT [17506] [4 00 PM] for pickup time).\n- Use CLICK [element_id] for buttons or checkboxes (e.g., CLICK [5363] for 'Like for Like' fuel policy).\n- Ensure all time and date fields are correctly formatted (e.g., '4:00 PM', '3:30 PM', 'April 16th').\n- If a step fails, recheck the element ID and value to ensure they match the current page state."
      }
    },
