      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Book the lowest priced auto train ticket for Mayank Raheja who is deep an need seat in lower level, is carrying a bike but has no service animal,needs assistance from Lorton to Sanford on June 10 between 12 to 6 pm.",
        "memory_description": "Booking task failed due to incorrect element selection during passenger information entry and missing steps for specifying travel details and assistance needs; correct by following precise UI interaction steps for form completion.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Web-based Train Ticket Booking\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the Amtrak homepage and click on 'Book Tickets'.\n2. Select the 'One-way' or 'Round-trip' option, then choose the route from Lorton to Sanford.\n3. Set the travel date to June 10 and time between 12 PM to 6 PM.\n4. Click on 'Passengers' and add one adult passenger named 'Mayank Raheja'.\n5. In the 'Passenger Details' section, select 'Lower Level' seating and check the 'Carrying a Bike' option.\n6. Ensure 'No Service Animal' is selected and check the 'Needs Assistance' box.\n7. Click 'Continue' and select the lowest priced available ticket that meets the criteria.\n8. Review the booking summary and complete the payment process.\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Use exact element IDs for form fields (e.g., TYPE [125796] [Raheja]).\n- Ensure all checkboxes (e.g., 'Carrying a Bike', 'Needs Assistance') are explicitly selected.\n- Confirm the travel date and time range before proceeding to payment."
      }
