      "payload": {
        "scenario_description": "Find a manufacturer-certified Chevrolet truck for sale within 10 miles of zip 42701, if found schedule a test drive for James Smith on April 17 at 4 pm.",
        "memory_description": "This is a web search and form-filling task where the agent failed to correctly identify and interact with UI elements, leading to incorrect actions and missed steps.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Web search and form-filling on KBB.com to find a manufacturer-certified Chevrolet truck within 10 miles of zip 42701 and schedule a test drive for James Smith on April 17 at 4 pm.\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the KBB.com vehicle search page.\n2. Use the search filters to select 'Chevrolet' as the make and 'Truck' as the vehicle type.\n3. Ensure the 'Manufacturer Certified' checkbox is selected.\n4. Enter the zip code '42701' in the location field and set the search radius to '10 Miles'.\n5. Click 'Search' to retrieve results.\n6. From the search results, select a vehicle that meets the criteria.\n7. Click on the 'Schedule a Test Drive' button or link for the selected vehicle.\n8. Fill in the test drive form with the following details:\n   - Full Name: James Smith\n   - Date: April 17\n   - Time: 4:00 PM\n9. Confirm the test drive request and ensure all fields are correctly filled.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Always verify that the correct element is selected before performing an action (e.g., clicking a button or typing into a field).\n- Use exact match syntax for actions, such as `CLICK [element_id]` or `TYPE [element_id] [value]`.\n- Ensure that all required fields are filled in the correct order and with the correct values.\n- Double-check that the test drive date and time are formatted correctly (e.g., 'April 17' and '4:00 PM')."
      }
    },
