        "scenario_description": "Show schedule for East Boston Ferry outbound Lewis Wharf and Long Wharf (North) stop.",
        "memory_description": "This was a web navigation task for retrieving a ferry schedule; the agent failed due to incorrect element selection and missing steps in the interaction flow, requiring a precise sequence of clicks and selections.",
        "content_body": "Task Type: Web Navigation (Schedule Retrieval)\n\nCorrect Workflow:\n1. Navigate to the MBTA website (https://www.mbta.com/).\n2. Locate and click on the 'Fares & Schedules' section (ensure correct element is selected).\n3. Select the 'Ferry' option from the menu.\n4. Choose the 'East Boston Ferry' route from the list of available options.\n5. Click on the 'Outbound' direction for the route.\n6. Select the stop 'Lewis Wharf' and 'Long Wharf (North)' from the stop list.\n7. Click the 'View Schedule' or equivalent button to retrieve the schedule.\n\nUI Interaction Rules:\n- Always verify the correct element is selected (e.g., using unique identifiers or text content).\n- Ensure that each action (CLICK, SELECT, TYPE) is applied to the correct UI element.\n- Use exact text matches for selections (e.g., 'Lewis Wharf' instead of partial matches).\n- If a step fails, re-evaluate the current page and re-identify the correct element before proceeding."
      }
